ai-health-prober is FOLDED into qnfo-ai-calibration (2026-10-06, PROBER-FOLD-1, agent_issues 1756, owner standing grant
OWNER-STANDING-GRANT-1 / charter decision rule 9; fleet_budget workers was 42 against a cap of 30).

The prober's code runs unchanged as the member proberMod inside qnfo-ai-calibration/worker.js (member version
2.3.15-folded): the host dispatches the "*/20 * * * *" cron to it, holds the Workers AI binding it probes with, and serves
its read routes at /prober/health and /prober/freshness (/prober/run needs the calibration key, because it spends Workers
AI). It still writes as WORKER = "ai-health-prober", so ai_model_health (read by qnfo-ai routing), freshness_guard (read by
qnfo-autonomy-scorer), fleet_heartbeat and capability_audit_snapshot keep their rows and readers.

This directory is kept for reference; the separate script is removed with cf-ops-actions delete-worker once the host is
verified running the member. canonical-deploy.yml skips any directory containing a RETIRED or FOLDED file. Un-folding is
a charter net-zero decision recorded in a PR that removes this file, never a way to get a deploy through.
